,\"rows\":[[\"31 Aug 2026\",\"3,610.88\",\"72.454\",\"3,538.426\"],[\"31 Jul 2026\",\"2,571.84\",\"51.59\",\"2,520.25\"],[\"30 Jun 2026\",\"4,968.77\",\"99.626\",\"4,869.144\"],[\"29 May 2026\",\"4,223.87\",\"84.698\",\"4,139.172\"],[\"29 Apr 2026\",\"5,419.4\",\"108.637\",\"5,310.763\"],[\"10 Apr 2026\",\"5,024.4\",\"100.777\",\"4,923.623\"],[\"27 Feb 2026\",\"4,466.84\",\"89.602\",\"4,377.238\"],[\"31 Jan 2026\",\"1,374.32\",\"27.551\",\"1,346.769\"],[\"31 Jan 2026\",\"1,932.92\",\"38.749\",\"1,894.171\"],[\"19 Dec 2025\",\"4,534.37\",\"90.923\",\"4,443.447\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1H43SYY631S0Z8YR\",\"t\":\"Vaulted Deep\"},{\"h\":\"https://350solutions.com\",\"t\":\"350Solutions\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biomass-geological-storage/1.1\",\"t\":\"Biomass Geological Storage v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biomass-geological-storage/1.0\",\"t\":\"Biomass Geological Storage v1.0\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H43SYY631S0Z8YR/prj_1HHYZFVGW1S044ZY/pjd_1K5FAGRQ41S0P42Y/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 18 Sep 2025\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1M0ACG4FJ1S02V0A?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H43SYY631S0Z8YR/prj_1HHYZFVGW1S044ZY/pjd_1M1BN9TN61S0P7T2/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H43SYY631S0Z8YR/prj_1HHYZFVGW1S044ZY/pjd_1M1BN9E5B1S0EY2R/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H43SYY631S0Z8YR/prj_1HHYZFVGW1S044ZY/pjd_1KYWFXC5D1S0AE73/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H43SYY631S0Z8YR/prj_1HHYZFVGW1S044ZY/pjd_1KYWFX0J21S034FS/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H43SYY631S0Z8YR/prj_1HHYZFVGW1S044ZY/pjd_1KWCE7X9A1S0QB7A/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nBICRS\\n1,000Y+\\nGreat Plains Organic Waste Sequestration\\nVaulted Deep\\nISSUED\\n70,234.61\\nBUFFER POOL\\n1,409.081\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n21 Aug 2023 to 20 Aug 2028\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nFeedstocks\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nVaulted deploys slurry injection technology to geologically sequester organic wastes for the purpose of permanent carbon removal. Vaulted owns and operates a built and permitted injection well site in Hutchinson, Kansas. This site hosts a network of 60 salt caverns, with the total capacity to hold 2-3 million metric tons of organic waste and room to expand beyond that. Vaulted secures a range of organic wastes (including biosolids, livestock and agricultural waste, paper sludge, and others) through sustainable sourcing practices from the surrounding area. Vaulted then minimally processes the waste on-site and geologically injects them, permanently (10,000+ years) sequestering the carbon.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\n01P4\\nApproval date\\n22 Dec 2023\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiomass Geological Storage v1.1\\nBaseline protocol version\\nBiomass Geological Storage v1.0\\nAccreditation\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nGreat Plains Organic Waste Sequestration\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n18 Sep 2025\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 5.91 tCO₂e removed from Great Plains Organic Waste Sequestration on 10 Aug 2026\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n5.908 tCO₂e\\nSequestrations\\n6.621 tCO₂e\\n-\\nActivities\\n384 kgCO₂e\\n+\\nCounterfactuals\\n329 kgCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nClark County Feeders\\tBiomass\\t29 May 2026\\nCity of Winfield_Biosolids\\tBiomass\\t11 Feb 2026\\nCity of Goddard_Biosolids\\tBiomass\\t11 Feb 2026\\nBuffalo Feeders\\tBiomass\\t17 Oct 2025\\nTiffany Cattle Co-Herrington_Old Manure\\tBiomass\\t30 Sep 2025\\nShowing 5 of 21\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n31 Aug 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n31 Aug 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n31 Jul 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n31 Jul 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n30 Jun 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 60\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n70,234.61\\nRetired\\n16,523.692\\nBuffer pool\\n1,409.081\\nCrediting period\\n21 Aug 2023 to 20 Aug 2028\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n31 Aug 2026\\t3,610.88\\t72.454\\t3,538.426\\n31 Jul 2026\\t2,571.84\\t51.59\\t2,520.25\\n30 Jun 2026\\t4,968.77\\t99.626\\t4,869.144\\n29 May 2026\\t4,223.87\\t84.698\\t4,139.172\\n29 Apr 2026\\t5,419.4\\t108.637\\t5,310.763\\n10 Apr 2026\\t5,024.4\\t100.777\\t4,923.623\\n27 Feb 2026\\t4,466.84\\t89.602\\t4,377.238\\n31 Jan 2026\\t1,374.32\\t27.551\\t1,346.769\\n31 Jan 2026\\t1,932.92\\t38.749\\t1,894.171\\n19 Dec 2025\\t4,534.37\\t90.923\\t4,443.447\\nShowing 10 of 252\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Vaulted Deep's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 1,409.081 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 1,465.017 certificates.\\n\\nVaulted Deep has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"